  "worked_solution": "Let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The trapezoid has a pair of parallel sides, $\\overset{―}{AB}∥\\overset{―}{CD}.$\n\n- Statement II is true. We can see that $∠ABC$ is a right angle, that is, $m∠ABC={90}^{∘}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The trapezoid has one pair of parallel sides, $\\overset{―}{AB}∥\\overset{―}{CD}.$ We can see that $\\overset{―}{AD}$ and $\\overset{―}{BC}$ are not parallel.\n\nIn conclusion, statements I and II are true.",
